{"answer": "Otto must pick the persona with `selectPersona(registry, message)`, and the selection has to be deterministic. It does a case-insensitive substring match of the latest customer message against each persona's `match` keyword list. It does not use a classifier call. When several personas match, it picks the one declared first. The function is pure and does no I/O. Its only inputs are the registry and the message text, so it takes no session, user id or customer number, and the same message always gets the same persona. It must never throw. For an empty message, a maximum-length message, a missing `defaultPersonaId`, or an empty `personas` map, it returns the default persona. If `defaultPersonaId` names no entry, it returns the first declared persona. If the map is empty, it returns an empty overlay under the default id. The selection runs inside `composePrompt`, which is called from the single `beforeModelResponse` hook. `composePrompt` builds the base prompt, then the chosen persona's overlay, then the dated line. It then writes the chosen persona's registry `id` to `session.activePersona` on every turn, fallback included.", "sources": ["docs/persona.md", "specs/support-agent-persona/spec.md", "issue-26", "issue-546"]}
```

